WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.981
Review sheet.

2
00:00:01.261 --> 00:00:06.872
Expect an initial loss near log C; if it’s much higher, the output layer is too confident.

3
00:00:07.152 --> 00:00:13.829
Saturated tanh passes back 1 minus t squared of the gradient, nearly nothing near plus or minus 1.

4
00:00:14.109 --> 00:00:26.291
Var(y) = fan_in Var(w) Var(x), so use weight standard deviation gain over sqrt(fan_in): gain sqrt(2) for ReLU, 5/3 for tanh.

5
00:00:26.571 --> 00:00:38.176
BatchNorm standardizes per feature over the batch, then scales and shifts; it makes the previous bias redundant, keeps running statistics for inference, and couples examples in a batch.

6
00:00:38.456 --> 00:00:45.880
Watch four diagnostics: activations, gradients, gradient-to-parameter ratios, and update-to-data ratios.

7
00:00:46.160 --> 00:00:49.829
Next lesson: compute every gradient in this network by hand.
